<title>JAPAN: Matsushita Electric comfortable w/110 yen.</title>
<headline>Matsushita Electric comfortable w/110 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matsushita Electric Industrial Co Ltd said on Thursday that the area of around 110 yen to the dollar is the foreign exchange level which is comfortable for its business.</p>
<p>Asked what a comfortable dollar/yen level would be, Matsushita Electric's director in charge of the European division, Seinosuke Kuraku, told reporters; &quot;Somewhere in the area of 110 yen could be the possibility.&quot;</p>
<p>In reponse to a question about whether Britain staying out of the European monetary and economic union (EMU) would work to Britain's disadvantage in terms of investment, Kuraku said Matsushita would not consider moving its production sites out of Britain only on the currency problem.</p>
</text>
